-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 15, DIVISION 1: COURT HEARINGS, rules 1 to 8 (roc3, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, a period it fixes in its own
--                words that has run out, an "if", "where", "unless" or "except" read as the text's no,
--                or "only".
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it limits a grant by its own wording (a scope with no
--                "only", a manner, a complement), is silent, or points outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Where a rule says "Subject to any written law" the input says whether a written law provides
-- otherwise; the written law itself is outside the sources.  O 3 r 2(1) is not threaded.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 15 -- Court hearings and evidence, Division 1 -- Court hearings (rules 1 to 8)`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- hearings in court and in chambers`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The kinds of matter paragraphs (1) to (3) sort.  An appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of
-- Appeal is its own kind, because paragraph (3) speaks of it (fork 15.1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `o 15 r 1 kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 15 r 1(1) an originating application`
    `o 15 r 1(1) a summons`
    `o 15 r 1(1) an assessment of damages`
    `o 15 r 1(1) a taking of accounts`
    `o 15 r 1(1) an appeal to a court other than the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`
    `o 15 r 1(2) a trial in an originating claim`
    `o 15 r 1(3) an application or appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`
    `o 15 r 1 any other matter`

-- src:1409 | 1. —(1) Subject to any written law or practice directions, every originating application, summons, assessment of damages, taking of accounts and appeal must be heard in chambers. (2) All trials in originating claims must be heard in open court.
@ref O 15 r 1(1) (src:1409)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 15 r 1 kind of matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 1(1) the kind of matter is one that must be heard in chambers` MEANS
    kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(1) an originating application`
    OR kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(1) a summons`
    OR kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(1) an assessment of damages`
    OR kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(1) a taking of accounts`
    OR kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(1) an appeal to a court other than the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`

@ref O 15 r 1(1) (src:1409)
GIVEN `kind` IS A `o 15 r 1 kind of matter`
      `a written law or the practice directions provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 1(1) the matter must be heard in chambers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`o 15 r 1(1) the kind of matter is one that must be heard in chambers` kind) AND `a written law or the practice directions provide otherwise` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law or practice directions"
        IF `o 15 r 1(1) the kind of matter is one that must be heard in chambers` kind THEN JUST TRUE
        IF kind EQUALS `o 15 r 1(3) an application or appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every originating application, summons, assessment of damages, taking of accounts and appeal" (fork 15.1: paragraph (3) speaks of these)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every originating application, summons, assessment of damages, taking of accounts and appeal" (any other matter)

