-- src:1420 | 3. —(1) All parties must attend the hearing of any matter in person (if they are not legally represented) or by a solicitor (if they are legally represented). (2) If a party fails to attend the hearing, the Court may dismiss the party’s application, action or appeal or make any other appropriate order against the party.
@ref O 15 r 3(1) (src:1420)
GIVEN `the party is legally represented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party attends in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party attends by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 3(1) the party attends as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the party is legally represented` AND `the party attends by a solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `the party is legally represented`) AND `the party attends in person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "All parties must attend the hearing of any matter in person (if they are not legally represented) or by a solicitor (if they are legally represented)" (a requirement read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

