        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the witness is a person confined in a prison"

-- src:1436 | (11) An order to attend court addressed to a person confined in prison is to include the following words: “ This order to attend court is sufficient authority as an order under section 38 of the Prisons Act for the Superintendent to produce the named person in court at the time and place stated.
