§§ `Rule 5 -- where the person to give evidence is out of jurisdiction`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1444 | 5. —(1) Where — ( a )
-- src:1445 | an application is made for permission for any person outside Singapore to give evidence by live video link or live television link in any proceedings; and
-- src:1446 | ( b )
-- src:1447 | the laws of the jurisdiction where the person is located require the issue of a letter of request to the relevant authorities of that jurisdiction for such evidence to be given,
-- src:1448 | an application may be made for an order in Form 30 for the issue of the letter of request.
@ref O 15 r 5(1) (src:1444-1448)
GIVEN `an application is made for permission for a person outside Singapore to give evidence by live video link or live television link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the jurisdiction where the person is located require the issue of a letter of request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(1) an application may be made for an order in Form 30 for the issue of a letter of request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an application is made for permission for a person outside Singapore to give evidence by live video link or live television link` AND `the laws of the jurisdiction where the person is located require the issue of a letter of request` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — ( a ) an application is made for permission for any person outside Singapore to give evidence by live video link or live television link in any proceedings; and" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1448 | an application may be made for an order in Form 30 for the issue of the letter of request.
@ref O 15 r 5(1) (src:1448)
`o 15 r 5(1) the form of the application for the issue of a letter of request` MEANS "Form 30"

-- src:1449 | (2) An application under this Rule may only be made in the General Division even if the proceedings are commenced in the State Courts.
@ref O 15 r 5(2) (src:1449)
GIVEN `the court in which the application is made` IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(2) the application may be made in the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court in which the application is made` EQUALS `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be made in the General Division"

-- src:1450 | (3) An application under this Rule must be made by summons and supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application and enclosing a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry pursuant to paragraph (4).
@ref O 15 r 5(3) (src:1450)
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit encloses a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(3) the application is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made by summons` AND `the summons is supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application` AND `the affidavit encloses a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made by summons and supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application and enclosing a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry" (a requirement of form and content read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1451 | (4) Where an order is made under paragraph (1) for the issue of a letter of request to the relevant authorities of a jurisdiction to permit evidence to be given by live video link or live television link by any person in that jurisdiction, paragraphs (5) to (8) apply.
@ref O 15 r 5(4) (src:1451)
