GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(4) paragraphs (5) to (8) apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order is made under paragraph (1) for the issue of a letter of request to permit evidence to be given by live video link or live television link` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under paragraph (1) for the issue of a letter of request" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

DECLARE `o 15 r 5(5) the form of the letter of request` IS ONE OF
    `o 15 r 5(5)(a) the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form`
    `o 15 r 5(5)(b) Form 17`

-- src:1452 | (5) The party obtaining the order must prepare the letter of request and file it in the Registry, and the letter must be — ( a )
-- src:1453 | in a case where the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be given is a jurisdiction to which the Hague Evidence Convention applies — in the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form; or
-- src:1454 | ( b )
-- src:1455 | in any other case — in Form 17,
-- src:1456 | with such variations as may be required by the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be given or by the order.
@ref O 15 r 5(5) (src:1452-1456)
GIVEN `the Hague Evidence Convention applies to the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 15 r 5(5) the form of the letter of request`
`o 15 r 5(5) the letter of request must be in` MEANS
    IF `the Hague Evidence Convention applies to the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be given`
    THEN `o 15 r 5(5)(a) the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form`
    ELSE `o 15 r 5(5)(b) Form 17`

-- src:1457 | (6) A letter of request filed under paragraph (5), or a document attached to the letter, must be accompanied by a translation of the letter or document in a language specified by the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be given, unless that jurisdiction accepts the letter or document in English.
