GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(6) a translation must accompany the letter of request or a document attached to it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `that jurisdiction accepts the letter or document in English` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that jurisdiction accepts the letter or document in English"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1458 | (7) Every translation filed under paragraph (6) must be certified by the person making it to be a correct translation; and the certificate must contain a statement of that person’s full name, address and qualifications for making the translation.
