    BRANCH
        IF `the party files in the Registry the documents mentioned in paragraphs (5), (6) and (7)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the party files in the Registry the documents mentioned in paragraphs (5), (6) and (7)" (a "when" that is not met, read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (c)))

@ref O 15 r 5(8) (src:1459)
GIVEN `the undertaking is signed by the party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is signed by the party's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(8) the undertaking is signed as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the undertaking is signed by the party` OR `the undertaking is signed by the party's solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "signed by the party or the party's solicitor" (a requirement of form read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- Rule 5(9): the four defined terms, each "means" (a closed definition).
DECLARE `o 15 r 5(9) defined term` IS ONE OF
    `o 15 r 5(9) Hague Evidence Convention`
    `o 15 r 5(9) issuing authority`
    `o 15 r 5(9) Recommended Model Form`
    `o 15 r 5(9) transmitting authority`

-- src:1460 | (9) In this Rule — “Hague Evidence Convention” means the Convention on the Taking of Evidence Abroad in Civil or Commercial Matters done at the Hague on 18 March 1970;
-- src:1461 | “issuing authority” means an authority responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule;
-- src:1462 | “Recommended Model Form” means a Recommended Model Form for a Letter of Request to be issued under the Hague Evidence Convention, as set out on the Internet website for that Convention at https://www.hcch.net/en/​instruments/conventions/specialised-sections/evidence;
-- src:1463 | “transmitting authority” means an authority responsible for transmitting a letter of request issued under this Rule to the relevant authorities of the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken.
@ref O 15 r 5(9) (src:1460-1463)
GIVEN term IS A `o 15 r 5(9) defined term`
GIVETH A STRING
`o 15 r 5(9) the meaning of the term in this Rule` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `o 15 r 5(9) Hague Evidence Convention` THEN "the Convention on the Taking of Evidence Abroad in Civil or Commercial Matters done at the Hague on 18 March 1970"
    WHEN `o 15 r 5(9) issuing authority` THEN "an authority responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule"
    WHEN `o 15 r 5(9) Recommended Model Form` THEN "a Recommended Model Form for a Letter of Request to be issued under the Hague Evidence Convention, as set out on the Internet website for that Convention"
    WHEN `o 15 r 5(9) transmitting authority` THEN "an authority responsible for transmitting a letter of request issued under this Rule to the relevant authorities of the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken"

@ref O 15 r 5(9) (src:1460)
GIVEN `the instrument is the Convention on the Taking of Evidence Abroad in Civil or Commercial Matters done at the Hague on 18 March 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(9) an instrument is the Hague Evidence Convention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument is the Convention on the Taking of Evidence Abroad in Civil or Commercial Matters done at the Hague on 18 March 1970` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Hague Evidence Convention” means the Convention on the Taking of Evidence Abroad in Civil or Commercial Matters done at the Hague on 18 March 1970"

-- src:1461 | “issuing authority” means an authority responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule;
@ref O 15 r 5(9) (src:1461)
GIVEN `the authority is responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 5(9) an authority is an issuing authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority is responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“issuing authority” means an authority responsible for issuing a letter of request under this Rule"

-- src:1462 | “Recommended Model Form” means a Recommended Model Form for a Letter of Request to be issued under the Hague Evidence Convention, as set out on the Internet website for that Convention at https://www.hcch.net/en/​instruments/conventions/specialised-sections/evidence;
@ref O 15 r 5(9) (src:1462)
