-- src:1486 | 8. —(1) Subject to any written law and unless the Court otherwise directs, the trial in an originating claim, assessment of damages or value, and taking of accounts must be heard by one Judge. (2) The Judge may hear the trial or part of the trial with the assistance of one or 2 assessors who must take such part in the trial and be remunerated in the manner and the amount that the Court orders.
@ref O 15 r 8(2) (src:1486)
GIVEN `the number of assessors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(2) the Judge may hear the trial or part of it with the assistance of assessors` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of assessors` EQUALS 1 OR `the number of assessors` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the assistance of one or 2 assessors"

-- src:1487 | (3) If none of the parties attends Court when the trial begins, the Court may dismiss the claim and any counterclaim.
@ref O 15 r 8(3) (src:1487)
GIVEN `none of the parties attends Court when the trial begins` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(3) the Court may dismiss the claim and any counterclaim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `none of the parties attends Court when the trial begins` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If none of the parties attends Court when the trial begins" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1488 | (4) If one of the parties does not attend Court when the trial begins, the Court may proceed with the trial or give judgment against or dismiss the claim of the absent party or make any other appropriate order.
@ref O 15 r 8(4) (src:1488)
GIVEN `one of the parties does not attend Court when the trial begins` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(4) the Court may proceed with the trial, give judgment against or dismiss the claim of the absent party, or make any other appropriate order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `one of the parties does not attend Court when the trial begins` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If one of the parties does not attend Court when the trial begins" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1489 | (5) The Court must have control over the order of proceedings and may give the appropriate directions before or during the trial and subject to such directions, the following order of proceedings set out in paragraphs (6) to (13) is to apply.
@ref O 15 r 8(5) (src:1489)
GIVEN `the Court has given directions that change the order of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(5) the order of proceedings in paragraphs (6) to (13) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court has given directions that change the order of proceedings` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to such directions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1490 | (6) The opening statements and affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief need not be read out in Court.
@ref O 15 r 8(6) (src:1490)
GIVEN `the Court has directed that they be read out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(6) the opening statements and affidavits of evidence-in-chief must be read out in Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court has directed that they be read out` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Court must have control over the order of proceedings and may give the appropriate directions"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be read out in Court"

-- src:1491 | (7) The claimant must begin and testify before the claimant’s witnesses.
@ref O 15 r 8(7) (src:1491)
GIVEN `the claimant testified before the claimant's witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(7) the claimant's evidence is given in the order the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant testified before the claimant's witnesses` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The claimant must begin and testify before the claimant's witnesses" (a requirement read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1492 | (8) The defendant and any other parties may cross‑examine the claimant and the claimant’s witnesses.
@ref O 15 r 8(8) (src:1492)
GIVEN `the person is the defendant or another party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(8) the person may cross-examine the claimant and the claimant's witnesses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the defendant or another party` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The defendant and any other parties may cross-examine the claimant and the claimant's witnesses"

-- src:1493 | (9) When the claimant and the claimant’s witnesses have completed giving their evidence, subject to paragraph (11), the defendant must begin and testify before the defendant’s witnesses.
@ref O 15 r 8(9) (src:1493)
GIVEN `the claimant and the claimant's witnesses have completed giving their evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant testified before the defendant's witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(9) the defendant's evidence is given in the order the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the claimant and the claimant's witnesses have completed giving their evidence`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the claimant and the claimant's witnesses have completed giving their evidence" (a "when" that is not met, read as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (c)))
        IF `the defendant testified before the defendant's witnesses` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant must begin and testify before the defendant's witnesses" (a requirement read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1494 | (10) The claimant and any other parties may cross‑examine the defendant and the defendant’s witnesses.
@ref O 15 r 8(10) (src:1494)
GIVEN `the person is the claimant or another party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(10) the person may cross-examine the defendant and the defendant's witnesses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the claimant or another party` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The claimant and any other parties may cross-examine the defendant and the defendant's witnesses"

-- src:1495 | (11) At the conclusion of the claimant’s case, the defendant may make a submission of “No case to answer”, in that the evidence in the claimant’s case has not made out a case requiring the defendant to make the defendant’s defence, on the basis that the following apply in relation to the defendant’s submission: ( a )
-- src:1496 | the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant’s witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant;
-- src:1497 | ( b )
-- src:1498 | the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant’s case or, if the defendant has such a counterclaim, the defendant withdraws it;
@ref O 15 r 8(11) (src:1495-1498)
GIVEN `it is the conclusion of the claimant's case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant's witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or withdraws it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(11) the defendant may make a submission of No case to answer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it is the conclusion of the claimant's case`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the conclusion of the claimant's case" (an occasion phrase with no trigger word: read as a scope limit (fork 15.7))
        IF (NOT `the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant's witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant's witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant" (a condition of the submission stated by "on the basis that the following apply": a defendant who will give evidence is outside it)
        IF (NOT `the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or withdraws it`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or, if the defendant has such a counterclaim, the defendant withdraws it" (a condition of the submission stated by "on the basis that the following apply": a defendant who keeps a related counterclaim is outside it)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1499 | ( c )
-- src:1500 | if there is more than one defendant and not all the defendants make the submission of “No case to answer” and the Court decides not to rule immediately on the submission of “No case to answer”, the defendant who makes the submission cannot rely on or make any submissions on the evidence given by any other party and cannot cross‑examine any party or witness who gives evidence after the submission was made;
@ref O 15 r 8(11)(c) (src:1499-1500)
GIVEN `there is more than one defendant and not all the defendants make the submission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court decides not to rule immediately on the submission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(11)(c) the defendant who makes the submission may rely on the evidence of another party or cross-examine a party or witness who gives evidence after it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is more than one defendant and not all the defendants make the submission` AND `the Court decides not to rule immediately on the submission` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot rely on or make any submissions on the evidence given by any other party and cannot cross‑examine any party or witness who gives evidence after the submission was made"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if there is more than one defendant and not all the defendants make the submission of “No case to answer” and the Court decides not to rule immediately on the submission"

-- src:1501 | ( d )
-- src:1502 | the defendant who makes the submission of “No case to answer” may rely on the evidence of the defendant’s expert and any other expert if those experts have already given evidence as a panel of experts during the claimant’s case;
@ref O 15 r 8(11)(d) (src:1501-1502)
GIVEN `those experts have already given evidence as a panel of experts during the claimant's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(11)(d) the defendant who makes the submission may rely on the evidence of experts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `those experts have already given evidence as a panel of experts during the claimant's case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if those experts have already given evidence as a panel of experts during the claimant's case" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

-- src:1503 | ( e )
-- src:1504 | the defendant who makes the submission of “No case to answer” and is unsuccessful may make submissions on the costs of the action.
@ref O 15 r 8(11)(e) (src:1503-1504)
GIVEN `the defendant's submission was unsuccessful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(11)(e) the defendant who makes the submission may make submissions on the costs of the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the defendant's submission was unsuccessful` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and is unsuccessful may make submissions on the costs of the action"

-- src:1505 | (12) At the conclusion of the evidence for all the parties, the Court must hear the submissions of all the parties in the order that the Court considers appropriate.
@ref O 15 r 8(12) (src:1505)
GIVEN `the evidence for all the parties has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 8(12) the Court must hear the submissions of all the parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the evidence for all the parties has concluded` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the conclusion of the evidence for all the parties"

-- src:1506 | (13) The Court may give its decision immediately after the hearing or at a later date.
@ref O 15 r 8(13) (src:1506)
`o 15 r 8(13) the Court may give its decision immediately after the hearing or at a later date` MEANS JUST TRUE
